   <narrative xml:lang="EN">TRUE COLOURS- HELP US KEEP ADESEWA&apos;S LEGACY ALIVE</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ADESEWA AME SENBANJO passed away on February 5, 2021 at age 19 from intra-cardiac lymphoma, an aggressive cancer of the heart.  Her death was a devastating experience for her parents, younger siblings and close family members.  Adesewa left behind a variety of artwork, drawings, two completed manuscripts of her unpublished books, video scripts and art illustrations. While alive, she had a note stuck to her bedroom door proclaiming her positive approach to life: &quot;LET YOUR TRUE COLOUR SHINE!</narrative>
  </description>
